/-!
# Structurality from `Equation3756` through a guarded companion

Generated by `defwork/itautcell.py`.  `Equation3756` is `x ◇ y = (y ◇ x) ◇ (z ◇ z)`.  Its guarded obligation
-- a bijection of a finite model commuting with the companion `if m(X,X) = Y then X else m(Y,X)`
is an automorphism -- is `GuardAut_pxx_y_x_pyx_Equation3756`, proved elsewhere.  That obligation
names no target, so every law the companion satisfies is another cell for free, and there
are 19 of them below.
-/

